-- חוק הסכמים קיבוציים, התשי"ז-1957 — sections 2, 15 and 16: the two kinds
-- of collective agreement, special and general, and whom each applies to;
-- and sections 19 to 23: what a collective agreement's personal provisions
-- are, and which provision governs when an agreement, a statute, an
-- employment contract or another agreement says otherwise. The text is
-- laws/collective-agreements-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר
-- החוקים הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-516).
--
-- The law ranks no kind of agreement above the other: a special agreement
-- and a general one that both apply to an employee meet in §23, as any two
-- agreements do. What §§15–16 decide first is whether an agreement applies
-- to the employee at all — and an agreement that does not is not one of the
-- agreements §23 compares.
--
-- Where a section says which provision is "לטובת העובד", the encoding is of
-- an amount the employee is paid, so the more favourable is the larger. A
-- provision that is not an amount (a duty, a procedure) is compared by a
-- reading, not by this file.

IMPORT prelude

§ `חוק הסכמים קיבוציים — הוראות אישיות ועדיפות`

DECLARE `agreement provision` HAS
    `is about terms of work, the end of work, or a duty or right of the employee and employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement applies to the employer and the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `changed or cancelled lawfully` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `2`

-- Two kinds: (1) a special agreement, for a particular undertaking or a
-- particular employer, between the employer (or an employers' organisation
-- representing it) and the representative organisation of the employees it
-- will apply to; (2) a general agreement, for the whole country or a part
-- of it, for some branches of work or all of them, between the
-- representative workers' organisation in the branch or area and an
-- employers' organisation there. What tells them apart is the reach the
-- agreement is made for.
@ref law:2
DECLARE `kind of collective agreement` IS ONE OF
    `a special collective agreement`
    `a general collective agreement`

GIVEN `made for a particular undertaking or employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `kind of collective agreement`
DECIDE `the kind of the collective agreement` `made for a particular undertaking or employer` IS
    IF `made for a particular undertaking or employer`
    THEN `a special collective agreement`
    ELSE `a general collective agreement`

§§ `15`

@desc An employee and his employer, as far as sections 15 and 16 ask whether a collective agreement applies to them.
DECLARE `employee a collective agreement may reach` HAS
    `his employer is a party to the agreement`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `his employer is represented for it by an employers' organisation that is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 15(2)
    `his employer was or became a member of an employers' organisation that is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc at the signing, or while the agreement is in force, in the branches or area it covers (section 16(2))
    `his employer was expressly left out of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 16(2)
    `he is of a kind of employee the agreement includes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is in an occupation or post the agreement includes` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A special agreement applies to (1) its parties; (2) the employers an
-- employers' organisation that is a party represents for it; (3) every
-- employee of the kinds it includes, employed by an employer that is a
-- party or is so represented, in the occupations or posts it includes.
@ref law:15
GIVEN e IS AN `employee a collective agreement may reach`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special collective agreement applies to the employee` e IF
        (   e's `his employer is a party to the agreement`
         OR e's `his employer is represented for it by an employers' organisation that is a party`)
    AND e's `he is of a kind of employee the agreement includes`
    AND e's `he is in an occupation or post the agreement includes`

`a collective agreement binds its own parties` MEANS TRUE

§§ `16`

-- A general agreement applies to (1) its parties; (2) the employers, in the
-- branches or area it covers, that were members of the employers'
-- organisation that is a party when it was signed, or became members while
-- it is in force, save members expressly left out; (3) every employee of
-- the kinds it includes, employed by such an employer, in the occupations
-- or posts it includes.
@ref law:16
GIVEN e IS AN `employee a collective agreement may reach`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general collective agreement applies to the employee` e IF
        e's `his employer was or became a member of an employers' organisation that is a party`
    AND NOT e's `his employer was expressly left out of the agreement`
    AND e's `he is of a kind of employee the agreement includes`
    AND e's `he is in an occupation or post the agreement includes`

GIVEN k IS A `kind of collective agreement`, e IS AN `employee a collective agreement may reach`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the collective agreement applies to the employee` k e IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a special collective agreement` THEN `a special collective agreement applies to the employee` e
    WHEN `a general collective agreement` THEN `a general collective agreement applies to the employee` e

-- Of either kind, an employee of a kind the agreement does not include is
-- outside it, whoever employs him.
`an employee of a kind it leaves out, of a party employer` MEANS `employee a collective agreement may reach` WITH
    `his employer is a party to the agreement`  IS TRUE
    `his employer is represented for it by an employers' organisation that is a party` IS TRUE
    `his employer was or became a member of an employers' organisation that is a party` IS TRUE
    `his employer was expressly left out of the agreement` IS FALSE
    `he is of a kind of employee the agreement includes` IS FALSE
    `he is in an occupation or post the agreement includes` IS TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` `an employee of a kind it leaves out, of a party employer`
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a general collective agreement` `an employee of a kind it leaves out, of a party employer`
#ASSERT `the kind of the collective agreement` FALSE EQUALS `a general collective agreement`

§§ `19`

-- "הוראות אישיות": the provisions on terms of work, the end of work, and
-- the personal duties and rights they set. They are deemed a contract of
-- employment between every employer and employee the agreement applies to,
-- and stay in force after the agreement itself expires, until changed or
-- cancelled lawfully — so expiry is no input here.
@ref law:19
GIVEN p IS AN `agreement provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a personal provision` p IF
    p's `is about terms of work, the end of work, or a duty or right of the employee and employer`

GIVEN p IS AN `agreement provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is part of the employee's contract of employment` p IF
        `is a personal provision` p
    AND p's `the agreement applies to the employer and the employee`
    AND NOT p's `changed or cancelled lawfully`

-- the closing words: taking part in a strike is not a breach of a personal duty
`taking part in a strike breaches a personal duty` MEANS FALSE

`a pay term` MEANS `agreement provision` WITH
    `is about terms of work, the end of work, or a duty or right of the employee and employer` IS TRUE
    `the agreement applies to the employer and the employee` IS TRUE
    `changed or cancelled lawfully` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `is part of the employee's contract of employment` `a pay term`
`a pay term changed lawfully` MEANS `agreement provision` WITH
    `is about terms of work, the end of work, or a duty or right of the employee and employer` IS TRUE
    `the agreement applies to the employer and the employee` IS TRUE
    `changed or cancelled lawfully` IS TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `is part of the employee's contract of employment` `a pay term changed lawfully`
#ASSERT NOT `taking part in a strike breaches a personal duty`

§§ `20`

-- A right a personal provision gives the employee cannot be waived: a
-- waiver of it has no effect, whoever signs it.
@ref law:20
GIVEN p IS AN `agreement provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a waiver of the employee's right under it has effect` p IF
    NOT `is a personal provision` p

#ASSERT NOT `a waiver of the employee's right under it has effect` `a pay term`

§§ `21`

-- A collective agreement may add to a right the statute gives the employee
-- and may not take from it: of a statutory amount and an agreement's
-- amount for the same right, the employee gets the larger.
@ref law:21
GIVEN `the amount the statute gives` IS A NUMBER, `the amount the agreement gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount that governs between statute and agreement` `the amount the statute gives` `the amount the agreement gives` IS
    max `the amount the statute gives` `the amount the agreement gives`

#ASSERT `the amount that governs between statute and agreement` 100 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `the amount that governs between statute and agreement` 100 80 EQUALS 100

§§ `22`

-- A term of the contract of employment that differs from a personal
-- provision of the agreement yields to it — unless the difference is in the
-- employee's favour and the agreement does not expressly forbid that change.
-- An amount: the contract's term governs only where it is larger and not
-- forbidden; otherwise the agreement's.
@ref law:22
GIVEN `the agreement's amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the contract's amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the agreement expressly forbids the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount that governs between agreement and contract` `the agreement's amount` `the contract's amount` `the agreement expressly forbids the change` IS
    IF      `the contract's amount` GREATER THAN `the agreement's amount`
        AND NOT `the agreement expressly forbids the change`
    THEN `the contract's amount`
    ELSE `the agreement's amount`

#ASSERT `the amount that governs between agreement and contract` 100 90 FALSE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the amount that governs between agreement and contract` 100 110 FALSE EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `the amount that governs between agreement and contract` 100 110 TRUE EQUALS 100

§§ `23`

-- Where more than one collective agreement applies to an employee, the
-- provision in the employee's favour governs: of two agreements' amounts,
-- the larger.
@ref law:23
GIVEN `the one agreement's amount` IS A NUMBER, `the other agreement's amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount that governs between agreements` `the one agreement's amount` `the other agreement's amount` IS
    max `the one agreement's amount` `the other agreement's amount`

#ASSERT `the amount that governs between agreements` 6 8 EQUALS 8

-- The section speaks only where more than one agreement applies to the
-- employee (§§15–16 say which do): an agreement that does not apply to him
-- is not weighed, however much it gives.
GIVEN `the agreements that apply to the employee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 23 weighs the agreements` `the agreements that apply to the employee` IF
    `the agreements that apply to the employee` GREATER THAN 1

#ASSERT NOT `section 23 weighs the agreements` 1
